From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:08:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] clutter/color: Add the HLG transfer function
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_HLG, appended to ClutterTransferFunction
so existing values keep their numbers, following Rec. ITU-R BT.2100-2:

 - Its default luminances are those wp_color_manager_v1 gives HLG:
   minimum 0.005, maximum 1000, reference white 203 and mastering
   maximum 1000 cd/m². A state may declare others; unlike PQ, the
   maximum is taken as declared, since it is the nominal peak Lw.
 - Decoding is a new color op, hlg_eotf, that sees the whole RGB
   vector: black level lift max (0, (1 - beta) E' + beta), the inverse
   OETF per channel to scene light E, then the OOTF
   F = Ys^(gamma - 1) E. F is display light normalized to Lw, the
   convention every other state uses for its linear values. With
   Lw and Lb the state's maximum and minimum luminance,
   gamma = 1.2 * 1.111^log2 (Lw / 1000) (the extended formula of
   Report ITU-R BT.2390, used for every Lw) and
   beta = sqrt (3 (Lb / Lw)^(1 / gamma)).
 - Black lands in the inverse OETF's square-root segment only while
   beta <= 0.5; beyond it decoding would invert, and at beta = 1
   encoding would divide by zero. One exported definition,
   clutter_luminance_get_hlg_parameters(), computes gamma and beta in
   double precision and refuses luminances that are not finite with
   0 <= Lb < Lw, or give beta > 0.5. The transform takes its parameters
   from it, clutter_color_state_params_new_full(), through which every
   parametric constructor goes, refuses such HLG luminances, and the
   Wayland creator will use it to fail them as 'unsupported'. It is
   listed in the symbols file.
 - Ys is the luminance of E in the state's own primaries. Its
   coefficients are the Y row of the primaries' RGB to XYZ matrix,
   from the new clutter_colorimetry_get_luminance_coefficients(),
   which accepts a colorimetry only if
   clutter_colorimetry_get_linear_bt2020_matrices() does, so it shares
   the single definition of a usable colorimetry. Because the OOTF
   depends on luminance, the op runs before the primaries matrix.
 - Encoding (HLG as a destination) is the exact inverse, hlg_inv_eotf:
   inverse OOTF (Ys = Yd^(1 / gamma), E = F Ys^(1 - gamma)) in the
   destination primaries after the matrix, OETF, then black removal.
   Scene light outside [0, 1] and the resulting signal clip.

Both ops have a CPU implementation, used by
clutter_color_pipeline_do_transform(), and a GLSL function with the
same maths; their parameters are uniforms. They are internal
(clutter-color-op-private.h, not installed or exported).

The parametric linear BT.2020 conversions now compute the matrices,
luminance coefficients and HLG parameters before adding the EOTF, so an
unusable colorimetry or HLG luminance range, which validated producers
never create, leaves an empty pipeline rather than one holding only the
EOTF.

CICP transfer characteristics 18 now map to HLG. HLG states need at
least 10 bits, and, like PQ, are blended in extended range gamma 2.2
sRGB when used as an output. Image description information reports
an HLG state as transfer_function.hlg; accepting HLG from clients is a
separate change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLZiLBYev72J1s4D37L7Bi
